  "patch_sha256": "3c081e1163a43ebaa62c06f203df558fb7a870b5893489e6fadf924e96062eae",
  "change": "find_limit treats a step that succeeds without moving as reaching the limit, so the SystemTime/Instant limit search terminates on clocks coarser than 1ns (Windows SystemTime: 100ns). saturating_add/saturating_sub compute the limit lazily (unwrap_or_else). Platform-neutral test assertions; coarse-clock regression test.",
  "reason": "On Windows the unpatched search never terminates; tor-netdoc calls saturating_sub while parsing every network-status consensus, so embedded Arti stalled at 15% bootstrap with one CPU core busy."
